From 8e6bb8a36b9c5a2cce1c3138aed50cb842121407 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bolgacg <bolgacg1@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:59:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Make the three other mow criteria configurable like
 mowThreshold

MIN_MOW_HEIGHT_CM, MIN_MOW_INTERVAL_DAYS and CRITICAL_COMP_INDEX were module
constants, so a trial could set the competition threshold but not the other
three criteria. apply_mow_decision now takes them as keyword arguments that
default to the same constants, so every existing caller behaves as before.

The trial config and POST /api/crop/trial-config accept minMowHeightCm,
minMowIntervalDays and criticalCompIndex next to mowThreshold; unset means
the rule default. The providers pass them through as mow_params. They join
the trial hash only when set, so existing trial hashes do not change.
The per-day criteria payload already carries each threshold, so the
persisted recommendation rows record the values actually used.
